    "body": "This specification, like many other web specifications, uses [Web IDL](https://webidl.spec.whatwg.org/) for its interface definitions. Therefore, by defining the parameter types of the `pipeTo` method [in the IDL of section 4.2.1](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#rs-class-definition), the Web IDL machinery will perform the appropriate type checks in the JavaScript bindings (and will throw a `TypeError` if they fail). Thus, these invariants are in fact fulfilled when `pipeTo` calls `ReadableStreamPipeTo`.\n\nThe reason why we still have these assertions is because we also expose [the \"pipe to\" algorithm](https://streams.spec.whatwg.org/#readablestream-pipe) for use by other specifications (e.g. fetch). In that case, it's the responsibility of the calling specification to make sure the inputs are correctly typed.",
